  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="8349-3c9a-48a9-f553" name="Albania (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>ALBANIAN ARMIES (Vlad the Impaler, pp.79-81): Albanian armies of the Princes and of Skanderbeg. Allies from other lists are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Albania]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 33%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  ALBANIAN ARMIES. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry 33-75% (must take 2+ units of Stradioti per 1,000 pts); Infantry up to 50% (must take 2+ units of Harketar; no more than 0-1 unit of Crossbowmen per 1,000 pts; handgunners may be taken after 1392, 0-1 unit may be used; one Mangonel or Top (Bombard) per 1,000 pts, bombards only in armies after 1392); Allies and Mercenaries up to 25% (Albanians may also select allies from Bulgar (until 1396), Epirote Byzantine (until 1340), Serbian (until 1458) and Italian Condotta from Armies of Chivalry; documented only). All allies are subject to the Allies and Mercenaries rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
